      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T23:35:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In AOSP CHRE, verifying that the endpoint (a nanoapp) exists on the MCU and can accept the offloaded socket requires changing thread context from the message thread to CHRE\u0027s thread, which is the reason for the async response. I think ensuring that an endpoint accepts a socket should be part of the \"open\" contract.\n\nI could also see this being useful for implementations that may need to send something from the MCU to the BT controller and wait for a response to accept a socket.",
